+# Registered staff draft preservation at browser support expiry
+
+Integration progress only. This qualifies one canonical Sales Contract editor
+registration and the shared staff HTTP error path; it is not universal form
+coverage, elapsed 24-hour acceptance or production admission.
+
+## Connected behavior
+
+The actual staff Axios response interceptor recognizes the proxy's original
+409 `API_BUILD_REFRESH_REQUIRED` before operational error normalization. It
+awaits explicit registered domain draft preservation, then rejects the same
+409 with a stable code and `PRESERVED` or `BLOCKED` evidence. It never navigates,
+retries, resubmits, reads arbitrary DOM fields or scrapes passwords/files.
+Existing error presentation displays the Persian result. No controls or visual
+layout were added.
+
+Fresh staff requests normally probe `/auth/me` before obtaining a business
+request lease. Expiry can reject that probe first. `BrowserSessionContinuation`
+therefore retains a copy of its last successfully acquired lease solely for
+local recovery. Reading it performs no network operation, and it cannot replace
+`acquire()` for server access. Current owner/generation must match; invalidation,
+accepted login or explicit clear removes it. An obsolete failure still cannot
+invalidate a newer generation. Without a proven local owner the result stays
+blocked.
+
+`BrowserBuildHandoff` takes explicit owner/workflow/draft/schema/base-revision
+registrations. It serializes all current domain payloads synchronously before
+the first await, calls the existing immutable strict IndexedDB archive with
+verified readback, rechecks session ownership throughout, then rechecks the
+registration set and exact current payloads. Unregistered, unidentified,
+foreign-owner, malformed, changed, failed or unreadable state cannot produce
+`PRESERVED`. Partially completed immutable archives remain available, but their
+partial result remains blocked. No original draft is cleared or migrated.
+
+The actual `CreateContractWizardClient` supplies its existing
+`buildContractAutosaveDraft` getter to `useContractEditRecovery`. The hook pins
+the latest committed getter in a browser layout effect and registers metadata
+from its existing recovery scope. It does not reuse a delayed checkpoint
+effect's stale payload. This preserves the existing product/modal/remaining
+stone/Stair System/payment recovery semantics. The existing explicit
+`reloadLatestRevision` handler continues its own archive-before-reload behavior.
+The server render uses a normal effect and produces no layout-effect warning.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- `browser-build-handoff-red-20261019.txt`: registry stub failed the actual
+  explicit owner-port preservation expectations.
+- `browser-build-handoff-green-20261019.txt`: shared owner-port behavior passed.
+- `browser-local-recovery-lease-red-20261019.txt`: missing local recovery seam.
+- `browser-local-recovery-lease-green-20261019.txt`: recovery lease boundaries
+  and registry checks passed.
+- `browser-build-handoff-unit-final-20261019.txt`: **12 passed, zero skipped**,
+  including current session/generation behavior, actual HTTP interceptors,
+  anonymous OTP identity separation, all-payload capture before async writes,
+  no registrations, foreign owner, malformed JSON, changed draft, partial
+  archive failure and owner invalidation.
+- `browser-build-handoff-native-browser-qualified-20261019.txt`: real Edge
+  Chromium, React Contract recovery hook, actual Axios/XHR, actual strict
+  IndexedDB/write/readback. A same-turn committed update is archived with its
+  latest value when the real session-probe endpoint returns expiry 409. The
+  original request remains rejected; business calls stay zero; no extra probe
+  or automatic navigation occurs. Unmounting the form yields blocked with zero
+  new archives. After refresh, fresh same-owner network authentication precedes
+  reading the exact retained bytes. Browser closed normally. Seven source
+  identities are checked before/after and printed in the raw receipt.
+- `browser-build-handoff-actual-contract-timestamp-red-20261019.txt`: a later
+  adversarial check used the actual `createContractAutosaveDraft` serializer.
+  The earlier focused fixture used a plain payload and missed that this actual
+  serializer stamps `updatedAt=Date.now()` on every capture. Consequently the
+  equality check incorrectly blocked an unchanged real Contract draft. The
+  original earlier PASS remains a limited plain-payload observation.
+- `browser-build-handoff-actual-contract-timestamp-green-20261019.txt`: registry
+  pins one capture timestamp before any await and reuses it for final domain
+  recapture. The actual wizard builder accepts that optional timestamp and
+  otherwise preserves its existing default current-time behavior. Actual
+  domain fields are still compared exactly; a changed field remains blocked.
+  The real browser fixture now uses the actual Contract serializer, recovery
+  schema 2 and latest committed state, passes, and prints eight exact qualified
+  source identities before/after normal browser closure.
+- `browser-build-handoff-contract-errors-final-20261019.txt`: existing Contract
+  mutation error semantics passed, with no SSR layout-effect warnings.
+- `browser-build-handoff-design-check-20261019.txt`: no new adoption violations.
+- `browser-build-handoff-design-foundation-20261019.txt`: **25 passed**.
+- `browser-build-handoff-design-adoption-20261019.txt`: **14 passed**.
+- `browser-build-handoff-frontend-typecheck-20261019.txt`: initial ES5 target
+  rejected Map spread; corrected to `Array.from` without changing compiler flags.
+- `browser-build-handoff-frontend-typecheck-final-20261019.txt`: typecheck passed
+  before the final SSR-safe effect alias. The later complete production build
+  `frontend-final-build-5b4cc688a771e5a9.json` passed compile, lint, final type
+  validation, 141/141 pages and immutable browser finalization with the actual
+  Contract timestamp correction. See `frontend-final-build-20261019.md` for
+  custody, expected generated configuration and preserved first-build failure.
+
+The browser HTTP identity/expiry endpoints are deterministic Playwright route
+fixtures, not production OTP or proxy/controller admission. The React hook,
+Axios interceptors, network adapter and IndexedDB implementation are actual
+application code. This does not claim the entire Sales wizard UI or every
+possible editable surface was exercised in this focused fixture.
+
+## Remaining registrations and transport connections
+
+No handler or browser storage may invent another workflow's draft semantics.
+Remaining owners include public applicant/mobile invitation forms; ordinary HR
+and personnel operations; partner contract creation/correction; CRM/customer
+operations; Accounting ledger and asset/treasury/tax operations; logistics and
+security workflows; support messages/files; inventory/master data; and user,
+department and administrative editing. Their owners must select serializable
+recoverable meaning, file handling, schema/version and same-owner restore
+behavior explicitly. Password/login/session-recovery fields must never be
+included in a generic archive.
+
+The direct native `<form>` scan finds 24 TSX files, but this is not the number of
+workflows: many ERP sheets/wizards use buttons and controlled fields without a
+native form. Form-tag counts therefore cannot certify complete coverage.
+
+Only the staff `api` response path is connected here. `browserScopedFetch`,
+anonymous public contracts, applicant Bearer-session forms and identity-only
+OTP verification need their own appropriate expiry/owner handling. They must
+not borrow a staff lease. Socket.IO generation ownership and native API asset
+requests remain independent pending connections. No global refresh handler or
+universal 24-hour draft guarantee is claimed.
+
