@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# ERP browser producer integration audit
+
+The initial missing expiry handler below is now partially connected for the
+registered staff Sales Contract editor. See
+`browser-build-handoff-20261019.md`; other form owners and transports remain
+unqualified. This inventory preserves the original finding's scope.
+
+Private integration progress; not 24-hour whole-platform acceptance or
+production admission. Repository snapshot inspected on 2026-10-19.
+
+## Direct transport inventory
+
+Runtime `frontend/src` TypeScript/TSX sources, excluding tests, contain five
+Axios instances after this correction:
+
+- `lib/api.ts`: authenticated `api`, identity-only `sessionProbe`, anonymous
+  `publicApi`. Each binds the immutable compiled browser producer identity.
+- `lib/hiringApi.ts`: applicant-session `applicant`, and now identity-only
+  anonymous `invitationVerification`. Internal hiring calls reuse `api`.
+
+There are three direct `fetch` expressions in two files:
+
+- `lib/browserScopedFetch.ts`: the authenticated browser branch binds producer
+  plus current user/session denial constraints; its server branch forwards
+  directly. Its one runtime consumer is the client-side Accounting dispatch
+  documents adapter (`features/accounting/dispatch-documents/dispatchDocumentsClient.ts`).
+- `lib/biometricConnector.ts`: intentional localhost hardware connector at
+  `127.0.0.1:47631`, outside backend release routing. Do not attach ERP session
+  or producer headers to this independent transport.
+
+No direct SSR route handler, server action or `getServerSideProps` HTTP producer
+was found in the scoped source scan. This statement is an inventory result,
+not proof of all dynamic runtime imports or native URL-producing components.
+No global fetch patch or broad replacement was introduced.
+
+## Corrected mismatch
+
+`applicantHiringAPI.verify` was the one direct global Axios request bypassing
+producer binding. The current `/apply` page could send its OTP verification
+to the legacy backend while later authenticated applicant requests selected
+the current browser's backend. The correction uses a separate anonymous
+identity-bound instance. It preserves effective URL, body, default credentials,
+timeout and JSON handling; it never reads the applicant token or acquires a
+staff session lease. The applicant-session transport remains separate.
+
+Meaningful transport regression:
+
+`node --import tsx --test src/lib/hiringBuildRequestIdentity.test.ts src/lib/browserBuildRequestIdentity.test.ts src/lib/browserSessionHttp.test.ts`
+
+Run from `frontend`. Three tests passed, zero skipped. OTP verification uses
+fresh child module processes for identified build, absent legacy identity and
+conflicting caller identity. The actual Axios adapter observes the effective
+URL/body, correct header, absence of applicant/staff authorization, unchanged
+credentials/timeout, and no transport call on conflicting identity. This is a
+frontend owner-port test, not a real OTP delivery/server acceptance test.
+
+Preserved observations:
+
+- `hiring-build-request-identity-red-20261019.txt`: actual OTP adapter received
+  no producer header for an identified build (null versus expected identity).
+- `hiring-build-request-identity-green-20261019.txt`: initial correction passed.
+- `hiring-build-request-identity-green-20261019-final.txt`: final typed child
+  environment and combined regressions passed. Scoped diff whitespace check
+  also passed. Whole-project typecheck remains root integration verification.
+
+Qualified source hashes:
+
+- `frontend/src/lib/hiringApi.ts`:
+  `6f105365635470f89da630db63e4194f7211c3c229b56c03e5455ee201a6f688`
+- `frontend/src/lib/hiringBuildRequestIdentity.test.ts`:
+  `00a8e023a2fa76ee83a233025b6717b76b8a7aeec8cf5283b7d69b83b61c52fd`
+
+## Remaining concrete integration gaps
+
+1. `hooks/useSocket.ts` creates Socket.IO with only `expectedUserId`, without
+   producer identity. Both private HTTP proxy variants reject `/socket.io`;
+   realtime needs its own genuine compatible backend/connection owner.
+2. `app/dashboard/security/reports/shifts/[slotId]/page.tsx:173` uses a native
+   `<img src="/api/security/shift-log/attachments/...">`. Such resource requests
+   cannot carry the custom producer header and therefore select baseline under
+   the current API selector. This literal direct API resource was identified;
+   dynamic native asset URLs still require complete ownership classification.
+3. No runtime frontend handler for `API_BUILD_REFRESH_REQUIRED` was found.
+   The versioned browser archive is currently integrated into sales-contract
+   `useContractEditRecovery.reloadLatestRevision`; it is not a universal
+   unsaved-form registry. A refused expired request can leave in-memory fields
+   intact, but this does not prove durable preservation before user refresh
+   across HR, public applicant, Accounting and other forms. Workflow-specific
+   draft ownership/serialization and verified archive-before-refresh remain
+   required; request interception alone cannot invent valid draft semantics.
+
+The actual identified Next artifact, API producer headers, real auth/session
+flows, retained assets/RSC, realtime, and expiration handoff must still be
+tested together through the final controller-owned update/rollback path.
