+# Final ERP frontend production build
+
+The final source integration completed the normal production build, including
+Next compilation, lint, complete type validation, 141/141 static pages, page
+optimization and the existing browser identity finalizer. This is build and
+compiled identity evidence, not production release or 24-hour browser support
+admission. No HTTP server or additional Compose service was started.
+
+## Final successful operation
+
+- Operation `5b4cc688a771e5a9`, original npm PID 40196, natural exit 0.
+- Browser/native identity `erp_online_final_20261019_5b4cc688a771e5a9`.
+- Logical output:
+  `frontend/.next-online-final-20261019-5b4cc688a771e5a9`.
+- Actual output:
+  `D:/sabalanerp-online-qa/frontend-build-workspace-5b4cc688a771e5a9/dist`.
+- Normal `npm run build`: existing 8192 MiB maximum heap and `cpus: 1`.
+  No skipped lint/type checks, compiler weakening, alternate Next entry,
+  `NODE_PATH`, production activation or deployment bypass.
+- Raw evidence `frontend-final-build-5b4cc688a771e5a9.json` and `.txt`; exact
+  generated configuration bytes `.tsconfig-before.txt` / `.tsconfig-after.txt`.
+
+The host had little C: capacity, so the owner-authorized fresh output junction
+points to one newly created D: workspace. Logical/physical paths and target
+device/inode were verified before and after. Installed Next cleanup code was
+inspected first: it deletes only entries beneath the output directory, does
+not remove the root junction and does not recursively follow child symlinks.
+The fresh output was empty. Its sibling `node_modules` junction points to the
+verified existing frontend dependency root, outside the cleanup target. Actual
+`createRequire` from the physical output resolves React JSX runtime and Next to
+exactly the same files as the canonical frontend package.
+
+The final raw report proves code inputs unchanged, finalized immutable browser
+and native BUILD_ID equality, healthy and unchanged full identities for all six
+existing local services, disk capacity before/after, actual output custody and
+natural original npm closure. A subsequent read-only WMI scan found no remaining
+Next/jest-worker Node descendants in the scoped build window.
+
+## Preserved first failure and configuration transformation
+
+Operation `211f53ba526d1366` compiled and passed lint/type validation, then failed
+collecting page data because Node resolved the actual D: output and could not
+find `react/jsx-runtime` in its ancestors. Its original code 1 report and output
+remain unchanged. The later successful operation uses a new workspace with the
+explicit sibling dependency junction; the failed run was not reclassified,
+resumed, pruned or adopted.
+
+Next's normal Windows configuration writer added each fresh output's
+`types/**/*.ts` include and sorted existing includes. The final runner permits
+only that exact include-set addition with all other parsed configuration equal.
+Both raw before/after files are retained; tracked configuration was not restored
+behind the original build. The initial explicit source guard omitted
+`frontend/next-env.d.ts`; it did not prove that generated selector unchanged.
+Its one changed route-type reference was subsequently qualified against the
+known-clean authored HEAD. No business code changed during qualification.
+
+After successful build and owner review, the ephemeral selectors were
+explicitly cleaned up so the Git candidate does not depend on private local
+output UUIDs. `frontend-final-build-config-lf-normalization-20261019.json`
+preserves the intermediate tsconfig line-ending normalization. The separate
+`frontend-final-build-generated-config-cleanup-20261019.json` and its four
+exact byte snapshots preserve and qualify the later cleanup: only the two
+known Next-generated include additions/order and the generated next-env
+route-type selector differed from clean HEAD. Both authored files now exactly
+match their original HEAD bytes. No generated output or historical evidence
+was deleted or altered, and no build was rerun during cleanup.
+
+This is a disclosed, reviewed post-build configuration change. Candidate
+selector bytes **do not match** the original generated build selector bytes;
+the raw successful build remains evidence for its actual generated inputs,
+with this supplemental qualification recording the canonical authored
+selectors separately. It is not a claim of a second build after cleanup.
+
+## Packaging boundary
+
+`prepareRetainedUiBundle` intentionally rejects symlink input roots and an
+artifact whose real path differs from its project path. That protection was
+preserved. This completed junction output therefore requires explicit verified
+materialization of its runtime bytes, or a separately reviewed physical-custody
+adapter, before use with that image packaging path. This build is not an image
+digest, retrievable recovery image, browser/proxy switch test or full restore.
+Existing canonical build artifacts were preserved.
