@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Retained proxy transitive source inventory
+
+New retained-UI diagnostic reports now capture `api-release-routing.mjs`, which
+the shared browser proxy imports even when only its UI transport is selected.
+A shared eight-module `proxyRuntimeSources` inventory drives both the report
+and a persistent physical-copy import regression. The test copies those exact
+bytes into a distinct temporary tree and imports the actual proxy/API exports
+without repository-relative fallback, network listeners or Docker operations.
+It checks captured source bytes remain unchanged and normally removes only its
+verified own temporary directory.
+
+New held-operation retirement checks the API dependency against its original
+captured hash. If an older report did not capture that dependency, current code
+that imports it refuses with `HISTORICAL_PROXY_DEPENDENCY_UNQUALIFIED`. No old
+receipt is updated, qualified retroactively or adopted; held operation bytes,
+unknown transport status and startup/retirement restrictions remain intact.
+This change does not run retirement or grant authority to restart an old run.
+
+Evidence:
+
+- `retained-ui-source-closure-red-20261019.txt`: missing API module in the
+  captured runtime dependency graph.
+- `retained-ui-source-closure-green-20261019.txt`: static closure checks passed.
+- `retained-ui-source-closure-qualified-20261019.txt`: actual physical copied
+  eight-module tree imported both proxy exports successfully, without Docker.
+- `retained-ui-source-closure-persistent-20261019.txt`: persistent regression
+  passed via `node --test --test-name-pattern 'copied retained proxy dependency'
+  tests/online-deployment/retained-ui-overlap.integration.test.mjs`.
+
+The expensive retained-image/Compose overlap fixture was not executed. Existing
+historical held operations were neither read for adoption nor mutated. This is
+dependency packaging verification only, with production admission unchanged.
